# Copy to .env and fill in the secrets. Keep it in bare KEY=value form:
# NO quotes, NO `export` (the Makefile sources it with a safe parser).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env
#
# The real .env is gitignored.

# Required — enables POST /api/v1/auth/steam (server secret, never client-side).
# Use the key from https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey (standard Web API key)
# together with the MANA_STEAM_API_URL line below — or a publisher Web API key
# (Steamworks partner site) if you prefer the partner endpoint.
MANA_STEAM_WEB_API_KEY=your-steam-web-api-key

# Comma-separated Steam app-id allowlist (alpha + demo).
MANA_STEAM_APP_IDS=3757600,4233280

# AuthenticateUserTicket endpoint. The server default is the partner node
# (https://partner.steam-api.com/...), which REQUIRES a publisher Web API key.
# With a standard key from steamcommunity.com/dev/apikey you must use the public
# endpoint instead (rate-limited). This line is safe for both key types.
MANA_STEAM_API_URL=https://api.steampowered.com/ISteamUserAuth/AuthenticateUserTicket/v1/

# Set to true to register POST /api/v1/auth/itch (itch.io web build login).
MANA_ITCH_ENABLED=true

# Google sign-in (Android multiplayer, docs/android-multiplayer.md) — set both
# to register POST /api/v1/auth/google. The client id is public (ships in the
# Android bundle; the server rejects tokens whose audience does not match it).
# MANA_GOOGLE_ENABLED=true
# MANA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Allowed browser origin(s): "*" or a comma-separated list. For the web build
# use the itch.io game-page origin, e.g. https://lfarroco.itch.io. Bearer-token
# auth (no cookies) means "*" is safe here — see server/README.md §CORS.
MANA_CORS_ORIGIN=*

# Optional: local server listen port, default 8787.
# MANA_SERVER_PORT=8787

# --- Client release-build vars (consumed by `npm run build` and the
# `make electron-build-*` targets — the Makefile sources this file, so setting
# them here bakes them into web AND Electron release builds). The server
# ignores these; they live here so one .env drives both the deployment and the
# release builds. See docs/building-and-running.md §Multiplayer auth
# configuration and docs/release-audit.md.
#
# Game-server base URL for released clients. LEAVE UNSET for local dev (the
# client falls back to http://127.0.0.1:8787). Set for the live game —
# otherwise shipped builds point multiplayer at the player's own machine:
# MANA_SERVER_URL=https://us-central1-mana-battle-f3b15.cloudfunctions.net/api
#
# itch.io OAuth client id for the web build (public — ships in the browser
# bundle; the same value is registered for the game's OAuth app in
# docs/itchio-auth.md). Empty disables browser multiplayer login:
# MANA_ITCH_CLIENT_ID=f20213f3887151a962afac88d0145c57
#
# Google OAuth client id for the web + Android builds (public — ships in the
# bundle; the same value must be registered server-side as MANA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
# and as an authorized redirect URI in Google Cloud — docs/android-multiplayer.md).
# Empty hides Google sign-in:
# MANA_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
#
# Android release signing (make android-build -> ./gradlew bundleRelease):
# set these to produce an upload-signed AAB. The keystore lives at
# android/key.jks (gitignored); MANA_KEYSTORE_PATH is relative to the android/
# gradle root. Without them the AAB builds unsigned (Play rejects unsigned
# uploads — sign via Android Studio's Generate Signed Bundle instead).
# Find the alias with:
#   "/Applications/Android Studio.app/Contents/jbr/Contents/Home/bin/keytool" \
#     -list -keystore android/key.jks -storepass <store-password>
# MANA_KEYSTORE_PATH=key.jks
# MANA_KEYSTORE_STORE_PASSWORD=your-keystore-password
# MANA_KEYSTORE_KEY_ALIAS=your-key-alias
# MANA_KEYSTORE_KEY_PASSWORD=your-key-password
#
# --- itch.io upload automation (make itch-publish -> phaser/scripts/publish_itch.sh) ---
# butler API key — an API key with source "wharf" from
# https://itch.io/user/settings/api-keys. Optional if you've already run
# `butler login` interactively — but REQUIRED in Docker mode (the default when
# butler isn't installed on the host). Treat like a password (full account access):
# MANA_BUTLER_API_KEY=your-butler-api-key
#
# --- Steam upload automation (make steam-publish -> steam/scripts/publish_steam.sh) ---
# STEAM_USERNAME is the Steam account with Steamworks access to the game +
# demo apps. It is not a secret, so it lives here. The account password and
# the Steam Guard code are NEVER stored — the publish script prompts for them
# on the TTY each run (or takes them from exported STEAM_PASSWORD /
# STEAM_GUARD_CODE for a non-interactive run). See steam/STEAM_UPLOAD.md.
# STEAM_USERNAME=your-steam-username
